{
    "topic": "inserting_data_with_query_part_3",
    "title": "Inserting Data with query() (Part 3)",
    "description": "A beginner walkthrough of writing INSERT statements inside a Model using $this->db->query(), passing values safely with bindings, and confirming the insert worked.",
    "congratsText": "You can now save new records into the database from a Model!",
    "objectives": [
        "Use $this->db->query() to run an INSERT statement inside a Model",
        "Pass values safely into a query using question mark bindings",
        "Return the result of an insert so the Controller knows what happened",
        "Check whether an insert actually saved a new row"
    ],
    "recap": [
        "$this->db->query() runs any SQL you write, including INSERT statements",
        "Question marks stand in for values, and the second argument supplies them in order",
        "Bindings keep user input from breaking or attacking your SQL",
        "query() returns TRUE or FALSE on an insert, and affected_rows() confirms the save"
    ],
